            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>15.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <description><![CDATA[<h2>Check and queue skill updates together</h2>
<p>Check all skills for updates in one action, queue available updates, and review the changes before applying them. Skills from the same GitHub repository now stay together in list and card views. Pinned versions and local changes keep their existing protections.</p>
<h2>Diagnose your setup through Agent Config Hub</h2>
<p>Your agent can ask FullHouse Doctor to check global tool configuration, installed MCP servers, skills, and model settings without calling models or starting MCP servers. The report distinguishes problems from checks it could not complete. Hub also lists MCP installations across all supported global hosts.</p>
<h3>Improved</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>Review MCP removal before applying it</strong> — Removing an MCP server now queues one operation through Review → Apply, including its connections in hidden tools. The server disappears from the library only after a successful Apply; saved definitions and tokens remain. Agents can also preview and apply removal through Agent Config Hub in read-write mode.</li>
<li><strong>Eliza quotas in CodexBar</strong> — The quota counter and menu bar icon have been removed from FullHouse; the app opens its main window, appears in the Dock, and quits when its last window closes. To see daily and monthly balances, reset times, and spending by model family, use CodexBar with the Eliza plugin. Install the plugin separately and add your Eliza token. <a href="https://a.yandex-team.ru/arcadia/classifieds/junk/instasergio/codexbar-eliza">Plugin and setup instructions · Arcadia</a></li>
</ul>
<h3>Fixed</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>Import skills from nested GitHub folders</strong> — Importing a skills.sh search result now finds skills stored in nested repository folders, including imagegen in openai/skills. If several folders match, FullHouse asks for a direct folder URL instead of guessing.</li>
<li><strong>Clearer accessibility in Review diffs</strong> — Added and removed lines in the Review diff now expose a single accessibility label each, avoiding duplicate announcements.</li>
<li><strong>Steadier MCP list during refresh</strong> — The MCP list no longer adds an extra background or blank space above the first row while statuses refresh.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
